{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): Hi, um, sorry, I got here early cause the parking was a mess and I didn't wanna miss this. My right ear won't stop ringing and it's kinda freaking me out.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right ear. How long has it been ringing?",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (PATIENT): It's been a month. Gets way worse when the room's quiet, like at night. Is it a tumor? I keep googling and I'm scared.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): A month. Worse when it's quiet. Does the ear hurt?",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (PATIENT): No, it's not painful. The hearing on that side is muffled though, like cotton stuffed in it. Am I going deaf?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Not from what you've said. Any drainage?",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (PATIENT): Never. Nothing comes out of it. Do I need an MRI?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): No MRI today. Is the room spinning?",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (PATIENT): Not really, just the ring and the muffling. I run the big presses at the plant, super loud, and I don't wear the ear muffs, boss is always yelling about it. Is that what did this?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Loud presses, no protection. Blood pressure today is 138 over 84, pulse 72. You still have the high blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (PATIENT): Yeah, for years. I take the water tablet every morning, 25 milligrams, the hydrachlorothiazide one. I do forget it some weekends though. Can that pill cause the ringing?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hydrochlorothiazide. Unlikely. Any drug allergies?",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (PATIENT): No, never. Not to pills. What about my job, can I keep working the presses?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): We'll get there. Any ankle swelling?",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. End of a long shift my ankles puff up. Is that the pressure, is it dangerous?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sometimes. Any fever?",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Cough?",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (PATIENT): Uh, no.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Weight up or down?",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (PATIENT): Umm, hard to say. Maybe a pound or two, I never get on a scale. Clothes fit the same, I guess.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (PATIENT): Oh, and my granddaughter had her spring recital last night, little blue dress, she rang this tiny triangle the whole time. We all stood up like she'd won something.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (PATIENT): Traffic was brutal too, accident on the 405, took me like an hour and ten just to get off the ramp, and it was pouring, my wipers are basically dead. You follow the Dodgers? They blew it again last night.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Let me look in the ears.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Canals are clear. Both eardrums look normal. No wax.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (PATIENT): So not an infection? I'm not gonna lose the hearing, right? And those fancy ear muffs, do they actually work or is that just the boss talking?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Drums are fine. This is tinnitus, most likely from the noise. I can't rule out some hearing loss until we test it.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (PATIENT): A test, like today? What if it's bad? Should I be scared? I have like a hundred questions and you're going so fast.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hearing test. I'll put in the audiology referral. Wear ear protection every shift at the presses. Not optional.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (PATIENT): Ok, ok, I'll wear them. When do I come back? If it gets louder do I just sit and wait?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Come back in six weeks with the results. If the ringing suddenly gets much worse, or you start spinning, come sooner.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (PATIENT): Six weeks. You're sure it's not a tumor? Just tell me one more time, please.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nothing on exam suggests a tumor. We'll see what the hearing test shows. That's it for today."
 ],
